In a one-to-many relationship, "one" side will always be parent entity and "many" side will be child entity.

In a one-to-many relationship, Foreign key will move towards "many" side only and that side becomes owning entity.
The other side becomes non owning entity.

The entity providing the primary key is the parent entity.

Owning/Non Owning is different from Parent/Child. 

Use parent repo to do CRUD operations. 